  "$models": "What a host pushes, by the Rust type that reads it. Each sample parses, and every key in it comes back out of the type: a key the type drops is a row that silently stays at its default. A producer may omit a key the type defaults. A push that answers a command carries that command's req verbatim: PairStatus the Pair's, WakeStatus the Wake's, PhasePush and GamesPush the FetchLibrary's.",
  "settings_extra_keys": ["gamepad_ui_enabled", "android.low_latency"],
  "$settings_extra_keys": "Keys of the Settings sample that ride Settings::extra, which is serde-flattened: top-level keys, never nested under \"extra\".",
  "codes": {
    "phase": ["connecting", "streaming", "failed", "ended", "reconnecting", "profile_gone", "awaiting_approval"],
    "stale": ["fresh", "waking", "offline"],
    "menu": ["up", "down", "left", "right", "confirm", "back", "secondary", "tertiary", "jump_back", "jump_forward", "ok_down", "ok_up"]
  },
  "$codes": "The integer codes a host passes, each list indexed by code (bridge::phase_code, stale_code, menu_code). A phase or menu code past its list is refused; a stale code past it reads as fresh."
